1
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:21,435
Oisin: There is a boat on the shore that was not there yesterday. Did the sea bring it, or did you?

2
00:00:22,625 --> 00:00:31,195
Niamh: The sea brings what a heart keeps asking for. You have stood on this cliff every evening for a year, looking west.

3
00:00:32,438 --> 00:00:42,108
Oisin: Only to see if the land is still there. My father's hall. The hounds. Three hundred years is a long time not to look.

4
00:00:46,062 --> 00:00:57,462
Niamh: Then go and look. Take Embarr, and stay in the saddle. Whatever they say to you, whatever you see, do not let your feet touch that ground.

5
00:00:58,688 --> 00:01:05,478
Oisin: One evening. I will count the waterfalls on the way back, and you will hear the number before dark.
